<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Karluk Yabgu</h1><p class="st-meta">756 CE – 840 CE (approx.) · capital Suyab</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A Turkic confederation that fought beside the Arabs at Talas and seized Suyab, preparing the ground for the Kara-Khanid Khanate.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karluks">Karluks</a> lived in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/altai-mountains">Altai</a> and joined the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uyghurs">Uyghurs</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basmyls">Basmyls</a> in overthrowing the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-turkic-khaganate">Second Turkic Khaganate</a> in 744. Driven west by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/uyghur-khaganate">Uyghur Khaganate</a>, they moved to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/semirechye">Zhetysu</a> region, and in 751 their defection to the Abbasid side helped decide the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-talas">Battle of Talas</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang China</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Led by a yabghu, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karluks">Karluks</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suyab">Suyab</a> and the lands of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/turgesh-khaganate">Turgesh Khaganate</a> by 766, ruling a mix of nomadic tribes and the Sogdian towns of the Chu valley. They controlled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk-road">Silk Road</a> routes between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transoxiana">Transoxiana</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim</a>, and Muslim geographers describe them as rich in livestock and towns. Some groups converted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> early.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/uyghur-khaganate">Uyghur Khaganate</a> fell in 840, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karluks">Karluk</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bilge-kul-qadir-khan">Bilge Kul Qadir Khan</a> proclaimed himself <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khagan">khagan</a>, an event many historians take as the founding of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kara-khanid-khanate">Kara-Khanid Khanate</a>, which absorbed the Karluk lands.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="nomadic confederation, 756 CE – 840 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">nomadic confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central Asia and the Steppe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:74.75%;width:1.67%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>756 CE – 840 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Suyab</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Bilge Kul Qadir Khan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Tengrism, Buddhism, Manichaeism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Karluk Turkic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/kazakhstan">Kazakhstan</a>, <a href="/countries/kyrgyzstan">Kyrgyzstan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Karluks, Qarluq Yabghu</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=798&amp;focus=karluk-yabgu" aria-label="Karluk Yabgu on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6500 657 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Karluk Yabgu lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6820 913L6820 913M6820 913L6820 915"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6820 913h0M6820 915h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6820 913h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6820 913h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Suyab. <a href="/atlas?year=798&amp;focus=karluk-yabgu">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
